Sorry, I misunderstood your question.
See http://www.faqs.org/docs/Linux-HOWTO/SRM-HOWTO.html#AEN34

>>> set os_type NT
<power-cycle>

You need to do this when dealing with the i960 RAC raid controller
also.

Usually both ARC and SRM are installed on every system and updated by
firmware updates, so you only need to change between them.

To go from nt/ARC is a bit more tricky, but it is usefull when the
battery is going low:

- Supplementary menu
- Set up system
- Switch to OenVMS or Digital Unix console
- Switch to Digital Unix

Kjell


