On the unit I bought, it came with both metal and plastic spools.  It
looks like the metal spools were a smaller diameter and older than the
plastic spools.  I got a couple plastic spools in their plastic
envelope, but 15+ years of sitting in the desert climate of Nevada has
dried out the ink even sealed in its plastic bag.  (The bag probably
has small holes in it.)  The ink is legible, but not the nice dark
color that a fresh ribbon always gave.  The previous owner never had
an LA-36, so I suspect that the ribbons can be interchanged between
the two without any fuss.  The only difference I can see on the spools
is that the metal spool has 4 holes to receive the pins that rotate
the spool, while the plastic spool has only 2 holes.  The LA-120 has
two pins and I don't recall the LA-36 as having 4 pins, but its been
25 years since I've seen an LA-36 in the flesh.
