>> Yes.  The main logic board does not support bootable CDs.  You will need 
>> to use
>> the 5-diskette Windows 2000 bootable set to start up the CD.
>>
>> Next, Install a supported video card in the system.  The main logic board 
>> has a
>> Cirrus Logic graphics chipset, and there are no Windows 2000 drivers for 
>> Cirrus
>> graphics chipsets.  I suggest either an ATI or Matrox PCI video card.
>>
>> Next, increase the amount of system memory.  If you can still find some 
>> 32MB
>> 72-pin SIMMs of the right specifications, fill up all the SIMM sockets.
>>
>> After that, the system should install and run Windows 2000 pretty well.
>>
>> Fortunately, all the add-on parts are now very cheap.  If you can't find 
