It's been a few years, but I *think* that you can use any old UPS - just as 
long as the UPS has a serial port. I also think it was a straight through 
cable as well. However, you only truly need the UPS in case of a crash since 
those units didn't have cache batteries like some of the other more 
enterprise arrays.

I know we used APC and Deltec UPSes here at work when we ran the RA3000s and 
didn't have issues with either of them.

