> particular issue is addressed.
> 
> I have a Microvax II (MMJ ports) an MMJ cable and a VT320 terminal with MMJ
> ports
> 
> regards


I'd start by looking at the cable:

To connect the Microvax to the VT320 (both DTE), we need the following
signal cross-over cable:

MMJ VAX----------MMJ TERM

  1 ---------------> 6
  2 ---------------> 5
  3 ---------------> 4
  4 ---------------> 3
  5 ---------------> 2
  6 ---------------> 1

Some of the cable's I've seen connect pin-1 to pin-1 etc, instead of the
desired inverse.

I've also seen MMJ connectors applied to ethernet cables, which have a
different cross-over.

You might also consider getting an RS-232 breakout box and looking at the
signals:

MMJ VAX----------Signal

   1 -----------> Data Terminal Ready
   2 -----------> Transmit Data (TX+)
   3 ------------ Transmit Ground (TX-)
   4 ------------ Receive Ground (Rx-)
   5 <----------- Receive Data (Rx+)
   6 <----------- Data Set Ready

Hooking the MMJ up to a terminal with a standard RS-232 port (DTE) looks
like this:

MMJ VAX --------- Terminal

   1 ------------>  20 (DTR TO DSR)

   2 ------------>  2  (Tx+ to RD)

   3 ------------+
                 +- 7 (Signal Ground)
   4 ------------+

   5 <------------  3  (TD to RX+)

   6 ------------+- 6  DSR + CD
                 +- 8
          
                 +- 4  CTS + DTE on Terminal Side
                 +- 5





