There are a lot of uVAX-II devotees over on comp.os.vms.

I haven't seen one for years, but I recall the console port not being an
MMJ, more likely either DB-9 or DB-25. There should be a paddle switch
nearby (break enable) and a rotary switch (console language select) as
well as a single character digital display (3 at the console, 0 when the
o.s. is running).

The OpenVMS FAQ includes uVAX-II info., including the pinouts, data
rates and formats:

