There wasn't even an internal version of SRM 7.0 for the XP1000.  5.9 was
the last one for this platform.  The alphalinux web page must be wrong.

>The reason I'm asking is for one,
>OpenVMS 7.3-1 is complaining, that the firmware doesn't meet the minimum
>requirements (or something like that).

The VMS message is a bug.  The firmware check is done via a look-up table,
which is organized by CPU type and system family.  XP1000 is the only
member of its family whose FW stopped at 5.9, so the table is wrong for
this system.  There's a VMS release note asking users to ignore the
message.

>The other thing is, I upgraded
>from SRM 5.6 (I think) to 5.9 the other day and ever since my
>Intraserver ITI-6221 (Dual-SCSI, Dual-NIC, VGA) isn't not only
>recognized anymore, but SRM even refuses to go through all checks and
>hangs at E7 during init. I'd really hate to waste such a fine board and
>I am sort of hoping that the 6221 is supported again in a later firmware
>version.

I don't know anything about this card, sorry.


